@startuml
!include https://raw.githubusercontent.com/proveo-ca/identity/main/proveo.puml
title Credential boundary — inject, strip, sentinel (firewall mode only)

participant "cmd/proveo run" as RUN <<app>>
participant "internal/provider\nDetect · Resolve" as PROV <<app>>
database "<stateDir>/inject/broker.env\n0600, outside every agent mount" as SECRET <<error>>
participant "proveo-egress\nMITM + internal/broker" as MITM <<app>>
participant "agent process" as AGENT <<app>>
participant "pinned provider host" as VENDOR <<cloud>>
participant "any other host" as OTHER <<cloud>>

RUN ARROW_MAIN PROV : detect provider from keys present
PROV ARROW_MAIN RUN : exactly one provider → broker on
RUN ARROW_ERROR SECRET : write real key (host-side)
RUN ARROW_MAIN AGENT : " ""-e ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=proveo-brokered"" \n""-e PROVEO_CREDENTIAL_BROKER_KEYS=…"" "
note over AGENT
  The agent holds a **sentinel**, not a secret.
  ""apply_broker_sentinel"" rewrites any residual value a
  mounted file re-loaded, so reading its own environment
  yields nothing usable.
end note

SECRET ARROW_MAIN MITM : read once at startup
AGENT ARROW_MAIN MITM : request (TLS decrypted here —\nthe only point where it can be)

alt destination == pinned provider
  MITM ARROW_CLOUD VENDOR : successLabel(inject real auth header)
else any other destination
  MITM ARROW_ERROR OTHER : errorLabel(strip authorization · x-api-key ·\nx-goog-api-key · api-key · proxy-authorization)
end

note over MITM
  **"Inject keys, never expose."** The real credential is
  confined to the broker hop. A key the agent read from a
  mounted "".env"" is useless for exfiltration at the
  network layer, because credential headers never leave
  toward a non-pinned host.
end note

note over RUN
  **Gate:** the broker arms only when exactly **one**
  provider is detected (or a manifest pins one). A
  multi-key environment leaves the agent with a sentinel
  and nothing behind it — indistinguishable from a bad key,
  so ""proveo run"" **warns** in that case, naming the
  detected providers. ""provider.DetectVars()"" is the
  superset to clear when arranging a single-provider run:
  it includes names that are detected but not brokerable
  (bedrock ""AWS_ACCESS_KEY_ID"", vertex
  ""GOOGLE_APPLICATION_CREDENTIALS""), so an unrelated cloud
  credential silently suppresses brokering.
end note

note over AGENT, MITM
  **Mode-bound.** ""broker""/""proxy"" cannot decrypt TLS, so
  they keep key-in-env behavior with honest warnings; a
  key in a *mounted* "".env"" is still readable as a file
  there. Full isolation = firewall + host-env provisioning.
end note
@enduml
